  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I understand the need to reduce the IK refresh rate of some users to save on resources, but Desktop user refresh rate has been terrible ever since IK 2.0 came out. It appears to be about 3 to 5 fps, which makes a ton of motion and things completely lost, limiting the expressiveness of desktop users and limiting things such as prop and pen movement. I get it, we don't need a super high refresh rate for desktop users, but the current refresh rate is too low. Upgrading to at least 12-13 fps would dramatically improve the IK for desktop users. I haven't mentioned IK refresh rate for Selfie Expression simply because there's already another post about that, but doing this simple upgrade in general would probably also solve that issue.",
